#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:133
msgid "What Interpolation to Use?"
msgstr "Katero interpolacijo uporabiti?"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:135
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The interpolation sets how the shape of the pattern should vary from dark to "
"light."
msgstr ""
"Interpolacija določa, kako naj se oblika vzorca razlikuje od temne do "
"svetlobe."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:137
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You will only have to worry about the interpolation in the case of the round "
"and elliptical dots and the line patterns, although if you use some "
"equalization mode the interpolation will look the same in the case of the "
"line patterns."
msgstr ""
"Za interpolacijo boste morali skrbeti le v primeru okroglih in eliptičnih "
"pik in črtnih vzorcev, čeprav bo interpolacija v primeru vzorcev črt enaka, "
"če uporabljate način izenačevanja."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:139
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So, in summary, change the interpolation if you use round or elliptical dots "
"to vary how they change shape when changing the brightness. If you use "
"linear interpolation the dots will look as black circles/ellipses that grow "
"radially until they cover the :term:`cells<Screen Cell>`. If you use the "
"sinusoidal interpolation, the round/elliptical dot pattern will change "
"*symmetrically*. This means that at low brightness values the pattern will "
"look as small white circles/ellipses and at high brightness values it will "
"look as small black circles/ellipses. At mid-brightness values the pattern "
"will look as a checkerboard."
msgstr ""
"Torej, če povzamem, spremenite interpolacijo, če uporabljate okrogle ali "
"eliptične pike, da se razlikujejo, kako spreminjajo obliko pri spreminjanju "
"svetlosti. Če uporabljate linearno interpolacijo, bodo pike videti kot črni "
"krogi/elipse, ki rastejo radialno, dokler ne zajamejo :izraz:'<Screen "
"Cell>celice'. Če uporabljate sinusoidno interpolacijo, se bo vzorec okrogle/"
"eliptične pike spremenil *simetrično*. To pomeni, da bo pri nizkih "
"vrednostih svetlosti vzorec videti kot majhni beli krogi/elipse, pri visokih "
"vrednostih svetlosti pa kot majhni črni krogi/elipse. Pri vrednostih srednje "
"svetlosti bo vzorec videti kot kontrolna plošča.</Screen>"

