#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:190
msgid "What Size Mode to Use?"
msgstr "Kateri način velikosti uporabiti?"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:192
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At the end of the day choosing what size mode to use is a matter of how many "
"size-related calculations you want to avoid, and this usually has to be with "
"the final medium you intend the image to be displayed on."
msgstr ""
"Na koncu dneva, ko izberete način velikosti, ki ga želite uporabiti, je "
"vprašanje, koliko izračunov, povezanih z velikostjo, se želite izogniti, in "
"to mora biti običajno s končnim medijem, ki ga nameravate prikazati na sliki."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:194
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you intend to print the image you are making, then you will find it "
"easier to set the :term:`cells<Screen Cell>` size in terms of resolution and "
"cell frequency. If you choose the same resolution as the resolution of the "
"image then you can easily map the frequency values to real-life measures."
msgstr ""
"Če nameravate natisniti sliko, ki jo izdelujete, potem boste lažje "
"nastavitev velikosti :term:'celice v smislu ločljivosti <Screen Cell>in "
"frekvence celic. Če izberete</Screen> enako ločljivost kot ločljivost slike, "
"lahko preprosto preslikate vrednosti frekvence v meritve realnega življenja."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:196
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if you just want to produce digital images, then you may "
"find it easier to work with pixel sizes directly, as they are easier to "
"compare to the image size. In the case you don't really care about the exact "
"size of the pattern, this mode allows you to easily try different sizes "
"while looking at the image to see the changes."
msgstr ""
"Po drugi strani pa, če želite samo proizvajati digitalne slike, potem boste "
"morda lažje neposredno delali z velikostmi slikovnih pik, saj jih je lažje "
"primerjati z velikostjo slike. V primeru, da vam v resnici ni mar za točno "
"velikost vzorca, vam ta način omogoča, da enostavno poskusite različne "
"velikosti, medtem ko gledate sliko, da vidite spremembe."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:199
#, fuzzy
msgid "Using the Align to Pixel Grid Options"
msgstr "Uporaba možnosti poravnave v mrežo pikslov"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:201
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This option is key to achieve the maximum :term:`cell<Screen Cell>` "
"regularity and to avoid moire patterns. Usually you won't have to change the "
"default values."
msgstr ""
"Ta možnost je ključna za doseganje največje pravilnosti :term:'cell' in "
"izogibanje <Screen Cell>moire vzorcem. Običajno vam privzetih vrednosti ne "
"bo treba spreminjati.</Screen>"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:203
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The downside of aligning to the :term:`pixel grid<Pixel Grid>` is that the "
"available range of transformations is reduced. So, if you want to use a "
"specific rotation, cell size or shear, but you can't achieve it with the "
"selected alignment options, you can try to upper every how many cells to "
"align using the sliders. Always prefer first changing those values than to "
"disabling the alignment. In fact, disabling the alignment has the same "
"effect as aligning the grid at infinity."
msgstr ""
"Navzdol poravnavanje z :izrazom:'mreža piksel' je v tem, da je razpon "
"transformacij, ki je na voljo, <Pixel Grid>zmanjšan. Če torej želite "
"uporabiti določeno vrtenje, velikost celic ali omejevanje, vendar ga ne "
"morete doseči z izbranimi možnostmi poravnave, lahko poskusite z drsniki na "
"zgornjih delih zbrati vse celice, ki jih želite poravnati. Vedno raje "
"najprej spremenite te vrednosti, kot da onemogočite poravnavo. Dejansko ima "
"izklop</Pixel> poravnave enak učinek kot usklajevanje mreže pri neskončnosti."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:205
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that the greater the distance between alignment points (with "
"respect to the :term:`screen grid<Screen Grid>`), the more likely the "
"appearance of moire patterns will be."
msgstr ""
"Upoštevajte, da večja je razdalja med točkami poravnave (glede na :"
"term:'screen grid'), večja bo tudi videz <Screen Grid>moire vzorcev.</Screen>"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:208
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Brightness & Contrast"
msgid "Using the Brightness and Contrast Options"
msgstr "Svetlost in kontrast"

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:210
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most of the time, to achieve the classical screentone/halftone look, you "
"will have to set the contrast slider to a high value and then change how "
"dark/light the pattern looks with the brightness slider."
msgstr ""
"Večino časa boste morali za dosego klasičnega zaslona/poltona videza "
"nastaviti kontrastni drsnik na visoko vrednost in nato spremeniti, kako "
"temen/svetlobni vzorec izgleda s drsnikom svetlosti."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:212
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At 100% contrast the shapes will look aliased, binary. This is the classic "
"approach to digital halftoning, since printers can only output black or "
"white (ink or absence of ink)."
msgstr ""
"Na 100% contrast oblike bodo videti aliased, binarno. To je klasičen pristop "
"do digitalnega poltoninga, saj lahko tiskalniki izstopajo le črno ali belo "
"(črnilo ali odsotnost črnila)."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:214
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you want sharp edges but also want antialiased edges, you can try "
"choosing a contrast value around 80% to 95%."
msgstr ""
"Če želite ostre robove, pa tudi antialiased robove, lahko poskusite iti "
"izbiro kontrastne vrednosti okoli 80% to 95%."

#: ../../reference_manual/layers_and_masks/fill_layer_generators/screentone.rst:216
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sometimes you will need to have extra soft shapes. For example, if you use "
"the screentone generator with the halftone filter, you better use a 50% "
"contrast and 50% brightness. The reason is that the halftone filter performs "
"its own contrast adjustment. You can take advantage of these soft shapes to "
"then apply your own contrast adjustment filter and achieve even more unique "
"looks as shown in the following image."
msgstr ""
"Včasih boste morali imeti dodatne mehke oblike. Če na primer uporabljate "
"generator screentona s filtrom poltona, je bolje, da uporabite 50% contrast "
"in 50% svetlost. Razlog je v tem, da poltonski filter izvede to je lastna "
"prilagoditev kontrasta. Te mehke oblike lahko izkoristite, da nato uporabite "
"svoj filter za nastavitev kontrasta in dosežete še bolj edinstven videz, kot "
"je prikazano na naslednji sliki."

